4c00fcc6-11ee-4d84-9530-719be689b1b4	13cf13e2-9d01-45a7-8a3b-1e343c3da877	Adoption Process	adoption-process	Learn about our simple adoption process and how to bring home your new best friend.	# Our Adoption Process\n\nThank you for your interest in adopting! We're excited to help you find your perfect companion.\n\n## Steps to Adopt\n\n### 1. Browse Available Animals\nCheck out our adoptable animals to find one that fits your lifestyle and family.\n\n### 2. Submit an Application\nFill out our adoption application with information about your home, experience, and preferences.\n\n### 3. Meet & Greet\nOnce approved, we'll schedule a meet and greet with your chosen animal.\n\n### 4. Home Check\nFor certain animals, we may conduct a home visit to ensure a safe environment.\n\n### 5. Finalize Adoption\nComplete the adoption paperwork and bring your new family member home!\n\n## Adoption Fees\n\nOur adoption fees help cover:\n- Spay/neuter surgery\n- Up-to-date vaccinations\n- Microchipping\n- Health examination\n- Deworming and flea treatment\n\n*Adoption fees vary by animal. Check individual profiles for specific fees.*\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Be at least 21 years old\n- Have a valid ID\n- If renting, provide proof of landlord approval for pets\n- All family members should meet the animal\n\n## Questions?\n\nContact us at [your email] or call [your phone number]. We're here to help!	\N	t	f	f	\N	4209791a-ad1f-4379-afcb-75a7e963cdfb	4209791a-ad1f-4379-afcb-75a7e963cdfb	2026-01-12 08:38:30.180367	2026-01-12 08:38:30.180367
0fa4a062-8597-44e4-9bdf-f0aa24bd3647	13cf13e2-9d01-45a7-8a3b-1e343c3da877	Foster Program	foster-program	Open your heart and home to an animal in need. Learn about our foster program and how you can help.	# Become a Foster Family\n\nFostering saves lives by providing temporary homes for animals in need. Whether for a few weeks or months, foster families are essential to our mission.\n\n## Why Foster?\n\n- **Save Lives**: Foster homes free up shelter space for more animals\n- **Socialization**: Animals learn to trust and live in a home environment\n- **Assessment**: We learn more about their personality and needs\n- **Rehabilitation**: Some animals need time to heal or decompress\n\n## What We Provide\n\n- All food and supplies\n- Complete medical care\n- 24/7 support from our team\n- Training and guidance\n- The joy of changing a life!\n\n## Foster Commitment\n\nFoster periods vary based on the animal's needs:\n- **Short-term**: 2-4 weeks (ideal for adoption-ready animals)\n- **Medium-term**: 1-3 months (for animals needing socialization)\n- **Long-term**: 3+ months (medical recovery or special needs)\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Secure, pet-friendly home\n- Time for daily care and socialization\n- Transportation to vet appointments if needed\n- Patience and commitment\n\n## Types of Foster Care\n\n### Medical Foster\nCare for animals recovering from surgery or illness.\n\n### Behavioral Foster\nHelp shy or fearful animals build confidence.\n\n### Maternity Foster\nCare for pregnant mothers and newborns.\n\n### Emergency Foster\nTemporary care during shelter capacity issues.\n\n## Ready to Foster?\n\nFill out our foster application to get started. We'll match you with an animal that fits your lifestyle and experience level.\n\n**Questions?** Contact our foster coordinator at [your email].	\N	t	f	f	\N	4209791a-ad1f-4379-afcb-75a7e963cdfb	4209791a-ad1f-4379-afcb-75a7e963cdfb	2026-01-12 08:38:30.180367	2026-01-12 08:38:30.180367
dedc634d-71e8-436a-9bd3-ca56280431f7	cf715a0f-ec10-4927-a763-baf8cdb0b1ec	Adoption Process	adoption-process	Learn about our simple adoption process and how to bring home your new best friend.	# Our Adoption Process\n\nThank you for your interest in adopting! We're excited to help you find your perfect companion.\n\n## Steps to Adopt\n\n### 1. Browse Available Animals\nCheck out our adoptable animals to find one that fits your lifestyle and family.\n\n### 2. Submit an Application\nFill out our adoption application with information about your home, experience, and preferences.\n\n### 3. Meet & Greet\nOnce approved, we'll schedule a meet and greet with your chosen animal.\n\n### 4. Home Check\nFor certain animals, we may conduct a home visit to ensure a safe environment.\n\n### 5. Finalize Adoption\nComplete the adoption paperwork and bring your new family member home!\n\n## Adoption Fees\n\nOur adoption fees help cover:\n- Spay/neuter surgery\n- Up-to-date vaccinations\n- Microchipping\n- Health examination\n- Deworming and flea treatment\n\n*Adoption fees vary by animal. Check individual profiles for specific fees.*\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Be at least 21 years old\n- Have a valid ID\n- If renting, provide proof of landlord approval for pets\n- All family members should meet the animal\n\n## Questions?\n\nContact us at [your email] or call [your phone number]. We're here to help!	\N	t	f	f	\N	10ddf568-fb2f-4af2-a9d9-344af1ca4862	10ddf568-fb2f-4af2-a9d9-344af1ca4862	2026-01-12 08:41:21.344932	2026-01-12 08:41:21.344932
ecca3045-b455-46ef-bcd1-c01432d2510e	cf715a0f-ec10-4927-a763-baf8cdb0b1ec	Foster Program	foster-program	Open your heart and home to an animal in need. Learn about our foster program and how you can help.	# Become a Foster Family\n\nFostering saves lives by providing temporary homes for animals in need. Whether for a few weeks or months, foster families are essential to our mission.\n\n## Why Foster?\n\n- **Save Lives**: Foster homes free up shelter space for more animals\n- **Socialization**: Animals learn to trust and live in a home environment\n- **Assessment**: We learn more about their personality and needs\n- **Rehabilitation**: Some animals need time to heal or decompress\n\n## What We Provide\n\n- All food and supplies\n- Complete medical care\n- 24/7 support from our team\n- Training and guidance\n- The joy of changing a life!\n\n## Foster Commitment\n\nFoster periods vary based on the animal's needs:\n- **Short-term**: 2-4 weeks (ideal for adoption-ready animals)\n- **Medium-term**: 1-3 months (for animals needing socialization)\n- **Long-term**: 3+ months (medical recovery or special needs)\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Secure, pet-friendly home\n- Time for daily care and socialization\n- Transportation to vet appointments if needed\n- Patience and commitment\n\n## Types of Foster Care\n\n### Medical Foster\nCare for animals recovering from surgery or illness.\n\n### Behavioral Foster\nHelp shy or fearful animals build confidence.\n\n### Maternity Foster\nCare for pregnant mothers and newborns.\n\n### Emergency Foster\nTemporary care during shelter capacity issues.\n\n## Ready to Foster?\n\nFill out our foster application to get started. We'll match you with an animal that fits your lifestyle and experience level.\n\n**Questions?** Contact our foster coordinator at [your email].	\N	t	f	f	\N	10ddf568-fb2f-4af2-a9d9-344af1ca4862	10ddf568-fb2f-4af2-a9d9-344af1ca4862	2026-01-12 08:41:21.344932	2026-01-12 08:41:21.344932
50941608-88c9-450a-95f3-e78257f80ff0	3a4c2321-6a54-41a4-acf3-a7f2ffe0c051	Our Team	our-team	Meet the Haseya's Team		[{"id": "block_1768664754882_6cih8tb0l", "gap": "medium", "type": "columns", "columns": [{"id": "block_1768664754882_xh58m4u3a", "width": 50, "blocks": [{"id": "block_1768664760473_gwx27sfwp", "alt": "Kelli Briscoe", "src": "/objects/3a4c2321-6a54-41a4-acf3-a7f2ffe0c051/animal-photos/6b32f3e3-060e-4636-903a-7a899d1d29ab", "type": "image", "width": "large", "alignment": "center"}]}, {"id": "block_1768664754882_4p41kmpaa", "width": 50, "blocks": [{"id": "block_1768664799269_vjpeu6mjn", "type": "paragraph", "content": "Kelli Briscoe founded Haseya’s New Beginning on December 28, 2018 with one mission: The purpose of Haseya’s New Beginning is to form a passionate team of individuals dedicated to helping animals that need us the most, including the sick, the starving, the Wild, the weak, and the unwanted. We want to take the biggest challenges that seem impossible, with God by our side, and make them possible by providing each one with medical care, a proper diet, love, and most importantly a new beginning.", "fontSize": "medium", "alignment": "left"}]}], "backgroundColor": "#dbfaf7"}, {"id": "block_1768664866366_1zs4fwtuh", "gap": "medium", "type": "columns", "columns": [{"id": "block_1768664866366_coxcuczj8", "width": 50, "blocks": [{"id": "block_1768664870821_hhsr1pnmo", "alt": "Lisa Hebert", "src": "/objects/3a4c2321-6a54-41a4-acf3-a7f2ffe0c051/animal-photos/608eab6a-35ac-4ca5-9e64-55cd5b2f46d4", "type": "image", "width": "large", "alignment": "center"}]}, {"id": "block_1768664866366_ecde18efe", "width": 50, "blocks": [{"id": "block_1768664934051_cmkzbrlzu", "type": "paragraph", "content": "Lisa Hebert is a quick learner and one of our hardest workers. She dedicates all her time to our horses and managing the adoption center Flawlessly! She is also our very first horse rescue, Owen’s foster mom. ", "fontSize": "medium", "alignment": "left"}]}], "backgroundColor": "#dbfaf7"}, {"id": "block_1768664973800_2bhkh8lnw", "gap": "medium", "type": "columns", "columns": [{"id": "block_1768664973800_t9d8nob04", "width": 50, "blocks": [{"id": "block_1768664978439_23wpa0kd2", "alt": "Tanya Foytlin Browne", "src": "/objects/3a4c2321-6a54-41a4-acf3-a7f2ffe0c051/animal-photos/fcf266c2-f430-4d61-9c65-a1f240708dd0", "type": "image", "width": "large", "alignment": "center"}]}, {"id": "block_1768664973800_9mrb64g5f", "width": 50, "blocks": [{"id": "block_1768665076940_x2iojhyjy", "type": "paragraph", "content": "Tanya Foytlin Browne is the Director of our Rayne shelter. She is a great member of our organization. Her love for animals is easily shown.", "fontSize": "medium", "alignment": "left"}]}], "backgroundColor": "#dbfaf7"}]	t	t	t	\N	c9f80047-4456-426b-9ee8-d1b15f7301b9	c9f80047-4456-426b-9ee8-d1b15f7301b9	2026-01-17 14:58:16.27875	2026-01-17 15:52:03.628
824cf97a-7466-44c6-87e6-7ec94b02173e	3a4c2321-6a54-41a4-acf3-a7f2ffe0c051	Terms of Use	terms-of-use	\N	# Terms of Use\n\n**Last Updated: January 23, 2026**\n\n## 1. Acceptance of Terms\n\nBy accessing or using the iRescue.life platform ("Service"), which is owned and operated by Haseya's New Beginning Animal Rescue ("Company," "we," "us," or "our"), you agree to be bound by these Terms of Service ("Terms"). If you do not agree to these Terms, you may not use the Service.\n\n## 2. Description of Service\n\niRescue.life provides software management tools for animal rescues, including intake management, adoption processing, and third-party integrations.\n\n## 3. User Accounts\n\nTo access certain features, you may be required to register an account. You are responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of your account credentials and for all activities that occur under your account. You agree to notify us immediately of any unauthorized use.\n\n## 4. Communications and SMS Messaging (Twilio Integration)\n\nBy providing your phone number and opting in, you consent to receive text messages (SMS) from us regarding your account, adoption applications, or rescue operations.\n\n- **Opt-In:** You provide consent by entering your phone number and checking the consent box on our forms.\n- **Opt-Out:** You may opt out of receiving text messages at any time by replying STOP to any message.\n- **Fees:** Message and data rates may apply.\n- **Frequency:** Message frequency varies based on your activity (e.g., application status updates).\n\n## 5. Payment Processing (Stripe Connect)\n\nPayment processing services for users on iRescue.life are provided by Stripe and are subject to the Stripe Connected Account Agreement, which includes the Stripe Terms of Service (collectively, the "Stripe Services Agreement"). By agreeing to these Terms or continuing to operate as a connected account on iRescue.life, you agree to be bound by the Stripe Services Agreement, as the same may be modified by Stripe from time to time. As a condition of iRescue.life enabling payment processing services through Stripe, you agree to provide iRescue.life accurate and complete information about you and your business, and you authorize iRescue.life to share it and transaction information related to your use of the payment processing services provided by Stripe.\n\n## 6. Third-Party Services and Content\n\n- **Petfinder:** Our Service may integrate with the Petfinder API. Use of Petfinder data is subject to Petfinder's Terms of Service. We do not claim ownership of content imported from Petfinder. You agree not to cache or store Petfinder data longer than necessary for immediate use and to respect all attribution requirements.\n- **Google Workspace:** Features integrating with Google (Gmail, Drive, Calendar) are provided for your convenience. Use of these features is subject to Google's Terms of Service.\n\n## 7. Acceptable Use\n\nYou agree not to use the Service to:\n\n- Violate any local, state, national, or international law.\n- Send unsolicited marketing messages or spam (in violation of Twilio A2P 10DLC policies).\n- Upload content that is infringing, defamatory, or harmful.\n\n## 8. Limitation of Liability\n\nTo the fullest extent permitted by law, Haseya's New Beginning Animal Rescue shall not be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including loss of profits or data, arising out of or in connection with your use of the Service.\n\n## 9. Governing Law\n\nThese Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the State of Louisiana, without regard to its conflict of law principles.\n\n## 10. Contact Information\n\nHaseya's New Beginning Animal Rescue  \n1321 Section Street, Rayne, LA 70578  \nEmail: haseyasnewbeginninghr@yahoo.com	\N	f	t	t	\N	c9f80047-4456-426b-9ee8-d1b15f7301b9	\N	2026-01-23 22:09:51.393267	2026-01-23 22:09:51.393267
20ee0d70-7e93-4b66-a0c6-d8c7f741426d	3a4c2321-6a54-41a4-acf3-a7f2ffe0c051	Privacy Policy	privacy-policy	\N	# Privacy Policy\n\n**Last Updated: January 23, 2026**\n\n## 1. Introduction\n\nHaseya's New Beginning Animal Rescue ("we," "us," "our") operating as iRescue.life, respects your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, and share your personal information.\n\n## 2. Information We Collect\n\n- **Personal Information:** Name, email address, physical address, and phone number when you register, apply for adoption, or donate.\n- **Payment Information:** Processed directly by Stripe; we do not store full credit card numbers on our servers.\n- **Google User Data:** If you choose to connect your Google account, we may access your Gmail, Google Drive, and Google Calendar data specifically to perform the actions you authorize (e.g., sending adoption emails, syncing rescue events, or storing files).\n\n## 3. How We Use Your Information\n\nWe use your information to:\n\n- Provide and maintain the iRescue.life platform.\n- Process adoption applications and donations.\n- Communicate with you regarding your account or requests.\n- Comply with legal obligations.\n\n## 4. SMS and Mobile Data Privacy (Twilio Requirement)\n\nWe value your privacy regarding your mobile information.\n\n- **No Sharing for Marketing:** We do not sell, rent, or share your mobile phone number or SMS consent status with third parties or affiliates for marketing/promotional purposes.\n- **Consent:** Mobile information will not be shared with third parties/affiliates for marketing/promotional purposes. All other categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this information will not be shared with any third parties.\n\n## 5. Google API Services User Data Policy (Google Requirement)\n\niRescue.life's use and transfer to any other app of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Google API Services User Data Policy, including the Limited Use requirements.\n\n- **How we use Google Data:** We only access Google user data (Gmail, Drive, Calendar) to enable user-requested features within the app.\n- **No Sale of Google Data:** We do not sell your Google user data to third parties.\n- **No Advertising:** We do not use Google user data for advertisements.\n\n## 6. Data Sharing with Service Providers\n\nWe share data with trusted third-party service providers solely to operate our Service:\n\n- **Stripe:** For payment processing.\n- **Twilio:** For sending SMS notifications (strictly operational).\n- **Petfinder:** For syncing animal data (if applicable).\n- **Hosting Providers:** To store and serve our application data.\n\n## 7. Data Security\n\nWe implement reasonable security measures to protect your information. However, no method of transmission over the Internet is 100% secure.\n\n## 8. Your Rights\n\nDepending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete your personal data. Contact us at haseyasnewbeginninghr@yahoo.com to exercise these rights.\n\n## 9. Changes to This Policy\n\nWe may update this Privacy Policy from time to time. We will notify you of any changes by posting the new Privacy Policy on this page.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Checklist for Compliance\n\nTo ensure these documents strictly protect you and pass third-party verifications (like Twilio A2P or Google App Verification), you must ensure the following:\n\n### Twilio / SMS Compliance:\n\n- On any form where you collect a phone number, you must have a checkbox that says: "I agree to receive SMS text messages from Haseya's New Beginning Animal Rescue. Message & data rates may apply. Reply STOP to opt out."\n- The "No Sharing for Marketing" clause in the Privacy Policy (Section 4 above) is mandatory for A2P 10DLC registration. Do not remove it.\n\n### Google Verification:\n\n- If you use "Restricted Scopes" (like reading a user's Gmail or full Calendar access), Google will manually review your Privacy Policy. They will look specifically for the Limited Use disclosure (Section 5 above).\n- The policy must be visible on your homepage footer.\n\n### Stripe Connect:\n\n- You must present the Stripe Connected Account Agreement link to your users (rescues) during their onboarding flow on your software.\n\n### Petfinder:\n\n- Ensure you display the "Powered by Petfinder" logo or text wherever Petfinder data is shown, as per their API brand guidelines.	\N	f	t	t	\N	c9f80047-4456-426b-9ee8-d1b15f7301b9	\N	2026-01-23 22:11:03.02801	2026-01-23 22:11:03.02801
